---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR } from '@/data/author';
import { personSchema } from '@/lib/seo';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description={`About ${AUTHOR.name}, the person behind saasmath.`}
  pathname="/about"
  jsonLd={personSchema()}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-10 prose-tight">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      saasmath is a set of free calculators and explainers for SaaS founders and operators.
      It exists because the good tools (Baremetrics, ChartMogul) are paywalled and the free ones
      (NerdWallet, SmartAsset) are for the wrong audience.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is built and maintained by one person. Nothing here is generated by an AI and
      shipped without a human reading it. Formulas cite the SaaS canon: David Skok, Brad Feld,
      Bessemer, Y Combinator, Carta. Where a formula is contested, the calculator says so.
    </p>

    <div class="not-prose flex gap-4 items-start mt-8 rounded-lg border border-ink-200 bg-ink-50/40 p-5">
      <img src={AUTHOR.photo} alt={AUTHOR.name} width="96" height="96" class="h-24 w-24 rounded-full object-cover bg-ink-100" />
      <div>
        <div class="font-semibold text-ink-900 text-lg">{AUTHOR.name}</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-ink-500">{AUTHOR.credentials}</div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-700 leading-6">{AUTHOR.bio}</p>
        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm">
          {AUTHOR.links.linkedin && <a href={AUTHOR.links.linkedin} rel="me">LinkedIn</a>}
          {AUTHOR.links.github && <a href={AUTHOR.links.github} rel="me">GitHub</a>}
          {AUTHOR.links.website && <a href={AUTHOR.links.website} rel="me">Website</a>}
          <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR.email}`}>{AUTHOR.email}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every claim about a metric cites its source.</li>
      <li>Every formula matches at least one authoritative reference.</li>
      <li>Calculators show the formula they use, not a black box.</li>
      <li>Errors are corrected in place with a change note, not deleted.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    <p>
      Not investment, tax, or legal advice. Not a substitute for a CFO or a lawyer. The math is
      the math; whether the input numbers are right is on you.
    </p>

    <h2>How the site pays for itself</h2>
    <p>
      Display ads (Google AdSense) and a small number of clearly disclosed affiliate links to
      tools the site actually recommends. No sponsored posts. No paid rankings.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
